  "comments": [
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63d05b4f_c7b8be84",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T09:32:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Q: What is the rationale here for rejecting a hypervisor granule that is smaller than the guest kernel page size ?",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7017b5b6_9a17cf8c",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1729538
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T12:59:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We only reject hypervisor granule sizes that are *larger* than the guest\u0027s own page size or not a power of two. I don\u0027t see that we\u0027re failing the init when the hypervisor page size is smaller than the guest\u0027s.",
      "parentUuid": "63d05b4f_c7b8be84",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "931bf01b_0b3bcbcc",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1782620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T14:15:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I spoke to Sebastian about this, it was just me being conservative since at the time we didn\u0027t have the case where the hypervisor\u0027s granule is larger.",
      "parentUuid": "7017b5b6_9a17cf8c",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "453c7c7f_47d719b1",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T14:26:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To Mark\u0027s point, I wanted to say that is **larger** not `smaller`.",
      "parentUuid": "931bf01b_0b3bcbcc",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef76bff5_2e6ad7f8",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T16:10:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the stage-2 page size is bigger than the stage-1 page size, we have to be careful not to over-share data with the host (e.g. from unrelated guest pages that happen to sit next to the one being shared).\n\nSo removing this check will mean we need extra logic on the share/unshare paths, where we might not be able to fail gracefully (and therefore may need to bounce the data?).",
      "parentUuid": "453c7c7f_47d719b1",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4c25423_c6db5298",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T16:22:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree to this point. This is something that pvmfw will have to enforce - validating that the DT presents the devices hypervisor page size aligned.\n\nWhat is your concern with share/unshare path ?",
      "parentUuid": "ef76bff5_2e6ad7f8",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f154e421_13376429",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T17:41:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Imagine we have a 16KiB stage-2 and a 4KiB stage-1. If the guest wants to share a 4KiB buffer with the host and we silently share 16KiB instead, then the host can now write to 12KiB of guest data that the guest did not want to share (and may include things like function pointers).\n\nSo the share/unshare logic in the guest should at least reject requests that aren\u0027t an exact multiple/alignment of the stage-2 page size.",
      "parentUuid": "a4c25423_c6db5298",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67789fae_a92b0e11",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-24T07:54:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can modify the `sharing/unsharing` hvcs to accept the number of bytes as argument and from there we can enforce the size of the share to be hypervisor PAGE_SIZE aligned. If it\u0027s not hyp PAGE_SIZE aligned then we can decline the request.",
      "parentUuid": "f154e421_13376429",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41fe50db_2bdc38e8",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-24T16:44:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/2969569 and friend already implement this for both MMIO_GUARD and MEMSHARE.\n\nThe \"granule\" size is stored and for every guest share/unshare guard/unguard, the guest makes sure the range is aligned with the granule size.\n\nThat gives a chance for the guest to succeed even though its page size is not aligned with the hyp\u0027s",
      "parentUuid": "67789fae_a92b0e11",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "36974fb4_cf851426",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/mm/ioremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-24T16:46:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(This is of course \"best-effort\")",
      "parentUuid": "41fe50db_2bdc38e8",
      "revId": "819734458e992c0c7ba1241e83bbf104496f8785",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
